{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "The camera coverage set: one CC0 sample per main camera maker and format from raw.pixls.us, beside the development samples in tests/fixtures/raw. `mise run fixtures` downloads them into tests/fixtures/cameras (never committed) and checks each file's SHA-256; the decode regression suite and the camera colour goldens check every one.",
  "gaps": [
    "Nikon's High Efficiency NEFs (HE and HE*, from the Z 8, Z 9, Z 6III, Z f, Z5 II and Z50 II) can't be decoded: LibRaw 0.22 reads only standard compression. They are refused as not supported yet (CAM-12).",
    "Bodies newer than LibRaw 0.22.2: the Sony A7 V is refused; the Sony A1 II decodes with a black strip along the bottom.",
    "No CC0 samples of the Leica M11, SL3 or Q3, or of iPhones after the 12 Pro.",
    "Sigma's Foveon X3F files, GoPro's GPR and JPEG XL mosaic DNGs aren't supported."
  ],
